  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Multipart singing of the Dorze, an Omotic-speaking people of the Gamo highlands around Chencha in southern Ethiopia, also known for their weaving. Groups of singers combine several distinct, overlapping voice parts in feast songs, work songs and spinning songs. Bernard Lortat-Jacob recorded the repertoire in 1974 and 1975; the recordings were issued by Le Chant du Monde and are held in the CREM-CNRS archives.",
